WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.750
A cat game on a phone asked

2
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:05.050
Grace for her name, her school,

3
00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:07.410
her birthday and a photo.

4
00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:10.260
Just to play a game about cats!

5
00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:14.060
Today: data about you, and

6
00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:15.020
what to keep private.

7
00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:19.050
Data about you is anything that

8
00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:20.490
tells people who you are.

9
00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:23.440
Your name, your age, your

10
00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:24.920
school, where you live.

11
00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:28.290
Your photo, your voice, your marks.

12
00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:31.080
Some data is fine to share,

13
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:32.700
like your favourite fruit.

14
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.660
Some needs care, like your photo.

15
00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:39.070
And some stays private: your address,

16
00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:41.810
your phone number and your passwords.

17
00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:44.940
Small facts add up.

18
00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:47.680
Your school, plus the time you

19
00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.380
walk home, plus your street.

20
00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:52.200
Together, a stranger could find you.

21
00:00:53.390 --> 00:00:53.870
Quick check!

22
00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:57.020
Which of these is fine to share

23
00:00:57.020 --> 00:00:58.180
with your whole class?

24
00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:02.160
Your favourite fruit: it says what

25
00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.020
you like, not where to find you.

26
00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:06.950
Addresses and passwords stay private.

27
00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:10.490
Before you type your details into a

28
00:01:10.490 --> 00:01:13.150
game, a website or an app, stop.

29
00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:15.950
Ask a trusted adult, like a

30
00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:17.310
parent or a teacher.

31
00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:19.630
And you can always say no.

32
00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.820
In the app, Lina is fourteen.

33
00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:26.790
Her six posts look harmless, but

34
00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:29.110
together they tell a stranger a lot.

35
00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:31.140
Choose who can see each

36
00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:32.660
post, and make her safe.

37
00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:34.470
Your turn.

38
00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:37.380
A website says: type your home

39
00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:38.780
address, and win a prize!

40
00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:40.410
What do you do?

41
00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:44.130
Stop, and ask a trusted adult

42
00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:46.410
first: a prize that wants your

43
00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:48.150
address is often a trick.

44
00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:52.190
Remember: data about you belongs to you.

45
00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:55.620
Some is fine to share, some needs

46
00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:58.220
care, and some stays private.

47
00:01:58.940 --> 00:02:00.840
And small facts add up.

48
00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:03.750
Try it tomorrow: with your

49
00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:05.930
family, draw three boxes on

50
00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:09.270
paper: fine, care and private.

51
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.320
Write ten facts about you, and

52
00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:13.660
sort them into the boxes.
